# toobur-veryfit-research — system overview
# A protocol lab notebook: captures in, notes and test fixtures out.
# Zones run left to right: entry points -> core -> state -> external.

title: |md
  # toobur-veryfit-research
  Reverse-engineering workspace for IDO / VeryFit watches sold as TOOBUR: three ways to capture BLE bytes, one canonical command map, and a test-fixture pipeline that feeds the Gadgetbridge driver.
| {near: top-center}

direction: right
grid-columns: 2
grid-rows: 2
horizontal-gap: 120
vertical-gap: 80

entry: Entry points {
  direction: down

  readme: `README.md` · the map: protocol reference first, then build and install, then probe usage
  live: `scripts/toobur_*.py` · live probe, v3 sync smoke, bind, dial, OTA, recover, bulk and bruteforce sweeps
  html: `htmlapp/*.html` · standalone Web Bluetooth panels, `confirmed-only.html` alone is 258 KB
  gb: `gadgetbridge/` · nested checkout of the working fork, 62 dirty files, its commits never leave that folder
}

core: Core {
  direction: down

  canon: `A200-PROTOCOL.md` · canonical wire command map, bruteforce and logcat backed, supersedes the scattered tables in `TOOBUR.md`
  parsing: `LATEST_SYNC_PARSING.md` · the v3 `0x05` then `0x04` route, save offsets, field layouts
  docs: `docs/*.md` · 14 topic notes: watch faces, OTA, dial commands, screen payloads, a recovery incident
  v3lib: `scripts/toobur_v3_sync.py` · pure builders and parsers: 137-byte `0x05`, per-type `0x04`, CRC16, channel guessed above 50 bytes
  pipeline: feature confirmation · logcat or probe hex becomes a fixture, a JUnit test, a `@ConfirmedFeature`, then a registry row
}

state: State {
  direction: down

  dumps: `packetdumps/` · logcat, live, synthetic, btsnoop and extracted captures {shape: cylinder}
  registry: `docs/confirmed-features.md` plus issues 001-020 and `bruteforce_results.txt` {shape: cylinder}
  functables: `func-tables/function_table.json` · capability bits lifted out of firmware {shape: cylinder}
  agent: `session-ses_f230.md` at 335 KB, `skills-lock.json`, `ralph/` · agent-run artifacts, not protocol truth
}

ext: External {
  direction: down

  watch: TOOBUR A200 over BLE · BlueZ D-Bus on Linux, Bleak when installed, the MAC defaults to the test unit
  phone: Android phone · adb logcat of VeryFit, or of the Gadgetbridge build under test
  chrome: Chrome Web Bluetooth · where the `htmlapp` experiments run
  fork: `d3nd3/gadgetbridge-veryfit` · where the driver, fixtures and migrations land
}

entry -> core: captures and questions
core -> state: notes, fixtures, registry rows
core -> ext: BLE + logcat

classes: {
  entry: {style: {stroke: "#2f6fbf"}}
  core: {style: {stroke: "#2f8f5f"}}
  state: {style: {stroke: "#a86a12"; stroke-dash: 3}}
  ext: {style: {stroke: "#8a4fbf"; stroke-dash: 5}}
}

entry.class: entry
core.class: core
state.class: state
ext.class: ext
